        "original_id": "f7b952c0-626c-5baf-8e74-fc6c496c16d1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Akira Yoshizawa, Hirohito\n- Concepts: Shōwa, wet-folding\n- Awards: Order of the Rising Sun\n- Topics: origami\n\nFacts:\n- Wet-folding is an origami technique developed by Akira Yoshizawa that uses water to dampen paper so it can be manipulated more easily.\n- In 1983, Emperor Hirohito awarded Akira Yoshizawa the Order of the Rising Sun, 5th class, which is one of Japan's highest honors.\n- Shōwa was the era name corresponding to Emperor Hirohito's reign, and Shōwa became Hirohito's own name after his death.",
